config VIDEO_HISTB_VENC
	tristate "HiSilicon HiSTB H.264 encoder driver"
	depends on ARCH_HISI || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on V4L_MEM2MEM_DRIVERS
	depends on VIDEO_DEV
	select VIDEOBUF2_DMA_CONTIG
	select VIDEOBUF2_VMALLOC
	select V4L2_MEM2MEM_DEV
	help
	  Support for the VEDU video encoder family on HiSilicon HiSTB
	  set-top-box SoCs. The encoder is stateful: a raw picture goes in and
	  H.264 network abstraction layer data comes out, with the parameter
	  sets and the slice headers written by the driver.

	  This backend serves the v2 VEDU of Hi3716CV200 and Hi3798MV100 -- the
	  part the vendor calls V2R8, built through its venc_v1.0 layer. It is
	  programmed with register writes and a 64-byte packet ring, and codes
	  IDR pictures only.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will be
	  called histb-venc.
